@Default settings override
This menu allows the world to override some of the settings specified in the
user configuration file. The user configuration file can contain a option to
prevent the default setting override from working, so it is not guaranteed
to use the override settings specified in the world file.

For each setting, you can specify whether or not the world can override the
setting in the user configuration file.

þ Speed: The normal game speed in milliseconds per frame. If the game is not
paused, then this will be the normal frame duration for the game.

þ Fast speed: The fast game speed in milliseconds per frame. This is only
used if F12 is pushed during the game.

þ Message timer: The number of frames during which the single-line text
message is displayed.

þ Menu position: The position of the F1 menu. The X position can be 0 to 39
and the Y position can be 0 to 8. (The X position is not used if the video
mode is forty columns.)

þ Game key repeat: Defines the behaviour when holding down a key during the
game play. If set to 0 then the normal key repeat delay and interval
applies. If set to 1 then the normal delay applies but the repeat interval
will use the game speed instead of the keyboard speed. If set to 2 then
it will start repeating using the game speed immediately with no delay.
